course: dictionary
lesson: 11087
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word wet can mean different things, so read the words around it to find the right one. «You never got wet.» Here wet means covered with water, because the sentence is about being soaked, not about the weather.
explain: «The roads were wet, so the cars needed much longer to stop.» Wet means rainy or covered with water here, because the cars need longer to stop on a slippery road. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: it still makes sense.
explain: Wet can also mean not yet dry, as in wet paint. Wet can even be a verb, meaning to make something wet. The words around the word always tell you which meaning you need.
fact: Wet is an adjective, a verb and a noun: wet, wetter, wettest; wet, wets, wetting; the wet.
fact: «Wet» means covered with or full of water, as in «wet hair».
fact: «Wet» can mean rainy, as in «a wet day».
fact: «Wet» can mean not yet dry, as in «wet paint».
fact: Water carries electricity, so never touch plugs or switches with wet hands.
exercise: «You never got wet.» What does wet mean here? | Full of sand | Dry and warm | Very fast | *Covered with water
exercise: «The roads were wet, so the cars needed much longer to stop.» What does wet mean here? | *Rainy or slippery with water | Hot and dusty | Quiet and calm | Full of sand
exercise: A sign says «wet paint». What does wet mean? | Very cold | Sold out | *Not yet dry | Full of water
test: A sign on the bench says «wet paint». Which meaning of wet is right? | Very fast | Covered with water | *Not yet dry | Rainy
test: Why should you never touch a plug with wet hands? | Wet hands are always cold | *Water carries electricity | Plugs are too small for wet hands | Water makes plugs heavier
exam: In «wet skin on very cold metal freezes and sticks to it», what does wet mean? | Not yet dry | Rainy and grey | *Covered with water | Sold out
